          "text": "Read: VISION, ROADMAP, SPEC §13.5/§7.5/§9.4, `openspec/specs/tool-calling`, issues #40/#213/#214/#215, and the live tool path (`tools/`, `runs/run-execution.service.ts`, `runs/snapshot-tool-execution.ts`, `runs/effective-context-resolver.ts`, `runs/run-stream-bridge.ts`, `chats/context-builder.ts`, `compaction/compaction.service.ts`, `instance-config/config-loader.ts`, web `chat-page.tsx`).\n\n## What's actually static\n\nThe issue reads like \"make tools dynamic.\" Most of that is already done. The **declaration** path is JSON-Schema end-to-end:\n\n```\nresolveEffectiveContext ──asSchema(zod)──▶ ModelToolDeclaration{id,description,inputSchema:JSONSchema}\n                                                    │ (immutable snapshot, hashed)\n                            ┌───────────────────────┴──────────────────────┐\n                            ▼                                              ▼\n       run-execution: jsonSchema(decl.inputSchema)          compaction: schemaOnlyTools(decls)\n                            │                                    (toolChoice:'none')\n                            ▼\n                  resolveBoundExecutableTools ──▶ TOOL********.get(id)   ◀── the only static part\n```\n\nThree Zod couplings to break, and one is a trap:\n\n| # | Site | Problem |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `tools/types.ts:58` `inputSchema: z.ZodTypeAny` | needs a JSON-Schema variant |\n| 2 | `tools/runner.ts:120` `inputSchema.safeParse(args)` | Zod-only validation |\n| 3 | `runs/snapshot-tool-execution.ts:83-92` | **rebuilds** `asSchema(executor.inputSchema).jsonSchema` and demands `canonicalJson` byte-equality with the snapshot, else `ModelContextExecutionError` → **fails the whole run** |\n\n(3) is the landmine. For an in-code registry, byte-drift means someone redeployed mid-run — failing loud is right. For a remote MCP server that re-advertises a tweaked schema between bind and execute, failing loud means **one upstream server edit kills unrelated ru